  "interpretation": [
    "Positive-centroid TF-IDF recovered more observed genre and topic assignments than the fixed frequency and label-name controls in this development diagnostic. Group-macro recall@3 was 85.30% for genres and 89.03% for topics versus frequency 52.40% and 26.32%. Eligible denominators are 353 and 379 groups respectively; unannotated facets are excluded, not counted as failures.",
    "All three methods and all four facets/cutoffs are retained. For the three-label audience facet, recall@3 and recall@5 are necessarily 100% and do not demonstrate ranking quality; inspect recall@1 and reciprocal rank instead.",
    "Label-macro recall@3 was 72.56% for genres and 80.06% for topics under positive-centroid retrieval. The erotica label has one training positive and no development positives; gothic_horror and games each have only two development positives. No sample expansion or hyperparameter selection was performed to repair rare-label coverage.",
    "Omitted labels remain unknown and no explicit negatives or human labels were created. These metrics cannot establish precision, false-positive rate, calibrated field output, reader mood or recommendation relevance. Literal genre words in blurbs are allowed available-input evidence.",
    "The subset excludes multi-record groups, all cross-source components and all source/effective role disagreements. This is a conservative 5120-record source subset, not verified full-work grouping or representative coverage of all books. The original test member was not opened; skipped allowed-member frames were streamed as bytes for integrity, not decoded.",
    "Independent recomputation verified train-only IDF for all 20000 features, reloaded all eight fitted sparse arrays and reproduced every ranking and score. The 32-record review queue was selected from training by a separate fixed hash before fitting and contains blank agent/human decisions."
  ],
  "next_actions": [
    "Use the bound 32-record training-only review worksheet to collect explicit source-supported positive/negative/unknown decisions. Keep review candidates separate from gold; do not infer negatives from synopsis silence.",
    "Implement a separately versioned source-conflict/adjudication path before using opposing reviewer assertions as supervised targets; the existing importer rejects source-positive conflicts and exported drafts must be preserved.",
    "Keep these lexical rankers as fixed controls for future neural or recurrent field models. Better known-label recovery alone is not a reason to deploy, scale RL, or claim recommendation gains.",
    "Once representative labels and work partitions are admitted, compare a supervised recurrent passage/session aggregator against pooling/order controls using the same inputs and budget. Current blurb recovery supplies neither ordered full-book passages nor reader-session rewards."
  ]
